# Applies to a build whose context is the repository root, which the three reactor services are:
# each builds one leaf of the Maven reactor and needs the parent pom beside it.  The other three
# built services, cassandra, accord-sql and frontend, name their own subdirectory, so this is the
# only ignore file in the repository.  Without it a root-context build uploads the working tree:
# .git alone is over a gigabyte here, because the Git LFS object store lives inside it.
.git
# A host build's output.  Copying it in would put a jar built against the host's JDK beside the
# one the image builds, and Maven would then decide which of the two to use.
target
**/target
.github
.claude
# Another service's vendored artefacts.  This build needs htap-cqlite/dist, which is 78.3 MB and
# is copied in the Dockerfile; the other two are 511.2 MB of Sidecar tarball and 176.5 MB of Ivy
# jars, of which 126.6 MB is one cassandra-analytics-core.  A root-context build uploads both
# unless they are named here.  The Python reader's 41.8 MB of wheels used to be a third and are
# deleted with that backend.
cassandra/dist
spark/ivy
cassandra-data
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
docs
workshop
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
.ci-tmp
.DS_Store
*.swp
